StaticOS: run ScummVM inside a sandboxed iframe with an opaque origin and no network.

An opaque origin has no IndexedDB and cannot fetch, so upstream's IDBFS mount and
its HTTP file nodes cannot work there. StaticOS's page hands the frame every file
through postMessage and puts them in the in-memory filesystem before main() runs,
then copies saved games back out the same way. So this build:

  - mounts nothing and fetches nothing at start-up (emscripten-fs-factory.cpp)
  - treats every path as an ordinary in-memory file, including /data
  - takes its arguments from the page, not from location.hash (custom_shell-pre.js)
  - does not ask for Web MIDI, which a sandboxed frame cannot use anyway (an empty
    midiOutputMap stays, because backends/midi/webmidi.cpp reads it)
  - exports FS and ENV so the page can reach the filesystem (configure)

